<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>07 · RESULTS (3/6) — H1, RE-TESTED</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Matching the data volume does not rescue H1
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', marginTop: 16, lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
        Tier 1 holds 8,055 and 3,796 rows; tier 2 holds 1,034 and 711. Tier 1 was downsampled to tier 2&apos;s actual
        <span style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontWeight: 'bold' }}> training counts — 497 and 723 rows, not the totals</span> — and both arms were retrained.
    </Text>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', width: 1128, marginTop: 18 }}>
        <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', background: '#16233A', padding: '11px 14px' }}>
            <Text style={{ width: 210, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Matched n</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 170, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', textAlign: 'right' }}>Λ, tier 1</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 170, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', textAlign: 'right' }}>Λ, tier 2</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 180, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', textAlign: 'right' }}>Δ</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 398, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', textAlign: 'right' }}>95% interval</Text>
        </Box>
        {[
            ['497 rows', '−0.041', '−0.008', '−0.033', '[−0.042, −0.024]', '#FFFFFF'],
            ['723 rows', '−0.104', '−0.016', '−0.087', '[−0.153, −0.022]', '#FFFFFF'],
            ['full data (reference)', '−0.098', '−0.012', '−0.086', '—', '#93A8C2'],
        ].map(([n, a, b, d, ci, color]) => (
            <Box key={n} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', padding: '13px 14px', background: '#0E1728', borderBottom: '1px solid #1D2A40' }}>
                <Text style={{ width: 210, fontSize: 18, color: color, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>{n}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 170, fontSize: 18, color: color, textAlign: 'right' }}>{a}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 170, fontSize: 18, color: color, textAlign: 'right' }}>{b}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 180, fontSize: 18, color: '#FF6B6B', fontWeight: 'bold', textAlign: 'right' }}>{d}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 398, fontSize: 18, color: color, textAlign: 'right' }}>{ci}</Text>
            </Box>
        ))}
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 40, marginTop: 22 }}>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 8 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#FFFFFF', fontWeight: 'bold', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
                Tier 1 stays below tier 2 at equal n, and both intervals exclude zero.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                The direction matches H1, so the confound is not what flattens ρ to zero: it explains part of the magnitude
                (full −0.086 shrinks to −0.033) but not the sign or the collapse.
            </Text>
        </Box>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 8 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#FFB020', fontWeight: 'bold', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
                The break is inside tier 3: +0.068 against −1.479.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                Two tasks in one tier sit at the top and the bottom of the ranking, so the correlation snaps there. Tier 1 vs tier 2
                is stable; tier 3 is undecidable.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC', width: 960, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>
            Limits: A4 refuses n-levels by design, so this row exists for A3 only; on tier 2 the graph arm loses rows (723 → 651),
            which biases Δ toward zero — the negative Δ is conservative. The full-data row is the mean of the same four tasks&apos; readings in lambda_ci.csv.
        </Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>10 / 18</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
